719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186287006 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534706 false] [17592186287007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304560 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304550 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1089 "q-11020" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/36a6f536866d34703f0900304a5859518461fdf0d8c1df42e5269a253c9c3ff2.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=2$, shown above." 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1113 #uuid "4167f5cf-9f6d-51bc-8664-d6f3f133f408" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304549 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{1}^{2}+7\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{1}^{2}-2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4})+7(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-2(2-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{49}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{41}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304551 13194139534706 true] [17592186304550 1000 #