ve $y={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304556 1113 #uuid "ee59a109-b2bd-5098-8f6c-967dab2c90fc" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304556 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{12}-(-\\frac{25}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304558 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304559 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1041 "field-1" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304559 13194139534706 true] [17592186304557 1110 #uuid "df52829b-59f8-5d84-90ef-64a9787ae8a4" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304558 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534706 true] [17592186304558 1111 #uuid "2465abe2-d60c-50de-ba70-347ec4490ee4" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304559 1034 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534706 true] [17592186304559 1111 #uuid "b9fba83f-4290-5b40-b396-bfcc44aeff34" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304560 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534706 true] [17592186304560 1111 #uuid "25f991f6-3353-56a2-83b3-1b27ebe7a8a4" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304562 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1089 "q-406820" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/31db08aa86f46d6601820b34dd938bc4b3738cba90f2fdd2721b4eb2069fa40b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1113 #uuid "1ce635ef-dd49-5b27-ab90-ab2605396353" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304561 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304563 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304564 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1041 "field-1" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304564 13194139534706 true] [17592186304562 1110 #uuid "96ab2319-8b24-5616-a0b6-4e7b27e531ba" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304563 1034 "2" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534706 true] [17592186304563 1111 #uuid "4cc25586-ebac-5b08-92c1-0da3e689842a" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304564 1034 "1" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534706 true] [17592186304564 1111 #uuid "797e665b-c83f-5bae-bfb9-18eaa7f1cfea" 13194139534706 true] [17592186304565 1017 #edb/ref 17592